## Why This Is Asked

This question probes understanding of idempotency, distributed transactions, and fault tolerance in real-time payment systems. It mirrors fintech patterns at Plaid and Lyft, where user actions must not duplicate or lose funds.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotency keys
- Outbox pattern and sagas
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once
- Dead-letter queues and backoff strategies

## Code Example

